# .pack-allowlist -- the ONLY list of what `make pack` puts in the .plugin archive.
#
# One path per line, relative to the repo root; a directory ships recursively
# (minus the junk patterns the Makefile recipe excludes). Anything not named
# here does not ship: docs/, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, README.md, CHANGELOG.md,
# tests/, eval/, plugins/, the budget files and every other maintainer file.
#
# Rule for adding a line: the path is read at run time by an agent, skill,
# command, hook or shipped script, OR the plugin format / the licence needs it.
# A document that shipped text has to open belongs under references/, not docs/.
#
# Guard: tests/test_pack_allowlist.py (CI gate #26) -- every entry exists, the
# Makefile recipe names no path of its own, and no shipped text file refers to
# a repo path that is not shipped.

# --- required by the plugin format / the licence
.claude-plugin/plugin.json
# marketplace catalogue: not read by a plugin host; kept because the shape that
# passed the Cowork drag-drop validator contained it (not re-testable in CI)
# -- remove this line and its EXEMPT entry once the user has tested a drag-drop without it
.claude-plugin/marketplace.json
LICENSE

